go over your work and use chromedevtools to go over the frontend when it comes to checking your work and testing and use tmux sessions and do this plan:

Plan: Real Historical Entry Prices for Position P&L

Problem Statement
Currently, entry prices are simulated instead of using actual historical data:

// src/app/page.tsx lines 200-201
const tqqqEntry = storedEntryPrices?.tqqq ?? marketData.tqqq.currentPrice * 0.95;  // FAKE
const sqqqEntry = storedEntryPrices?.sqqq ?? marketData.sqqq.currentPrice * 1.08;  // FAKE

This creates misleading P&L (+5% TQQQ, -8% SQQQ) that doesn't reflect reality.

Solution
When user sets an entry date, fetch actual closing prices for TQQQ/SQQQ on that date.

---
Critical Clarifications (from double-check review)

Two Distinct Use Cases
1. "Update" Button = Enter position NOW at current market prices (unchanged)
2. Date Picker = Simulate "what if I entered on this past date" (NEW feature)

Persistence Flow
After fetching historical prices, they MUST be saved to:
- storedEntryPrices state
- localStorage.entryPrices

This ensures prices survive page refresh.

---
